      "claim": "Transferable human gold contexts for small polar basic amide-containing molecules report absolute oral bioavailability at or above 22%: pramipexole >90% (C01), 5-HTP 49% (C11), labetalol 33% normal and 63% cirrhotic (C16, C13), ebastine about 40% (C02), PF-05241328 38% (C03, C08), and AZD0837 22-55% (C04, C14).",
      "card_ids": ["C01","C11","C13","C16","C02","C03","C08","C04","C14"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "The only sub-20% value in the source domains is isradipine normal-condition F of 16% (C20), but the context gold is cirrhotic F=37% (C06, C09) and isradipine is structurally dissimilar to the query, so it does not affirm F below 20% for the query.",
      "card_ids": ["C20","C06","C09"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L6 hepatic clearance records are for reference molecules, not the query; the closest structural analogs with a primary benzamide and N-methylamine (M02-M04) show low-to-moderate human liver microsomal intrinsic clearance of 8 µL/min/mg (C71, C65, C68), and a related benzamide shows low clearance (C63), so no record affirms high first-pass hepatic loss for the query.",
      "card_ids": ["C71","C65","C68","C63"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "hepatic_clearance_metabolic_stability",
      "applicability": "low",
      "direction": "neutral_or_unclear",
      "decision_effect": "no_change",
      "card_ids": ["C62","C63","C64","C65","C66","C67","C68","C69","C70","C71","C72","C73"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct absolute oral bioavailability measurement for the query molecule.",
    "No query-specific matched oral-versus-IV AUC or Cmax comparison.",
    "No query-specific hepatic clearance or metabolic stability measurement; L6 records are for reference molecules only.",
    "Query passive permeability and transporter status are not directly measured.",
    "Some high-F gold contexts are cirrhotic (labetalol, isradipine) and normal-condition values differ."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "L6 adds only reference-molecule hepatic clearance and metabolic stability records; the closest structural analogs show low-to-moderate intrinsic clearance, not high first-pass loss, and no record provides affirmative evidence for F below 20% for the query. The L1/L2 gold pattern of F at or above 22% for small polar basic amide-containing molecules remains the strongest endpoint evidence, so prediction stays high with moderate confidence."
}

